# Never wipe databases

Do **not** delete, reset, recreate-from-parent, truncate, or otherwise destroy
database data — including Neon preview / branch databases — to unblock
migrations, CI, deploys, or debugging.

## Forbidden without an explicit human decision outside this agent

- `delete-branch` / reset-branch on Neon (or any host) as a routine CI step
- Dropping schemas/tables, `TRUNCATE`, or re-seed that destroys existing rows
  to make migrate succeed
- “Just recreate the preview DB from main” as a default recovery path

## What to do instead

- Fix the migration / journal drift
- Add a forward migration
- Fail the job loudly and stop
- Ask the human if recovery truly requires a destructive reset

A cancelled preview deploy pointing at a bad URL is still better than silently
destroying data. Preview DBs often hold real session/profile state.
